 of them are not  filled so that's one in eight of the  jobs in food and drink from the farm  right way through manufacturing retail  and hospitality are not filled and  that's about half the vacancies in the  uk workforce now as long as those people  aren't there there will be impacts one  of those impacts will be disruption in  supply  and it depends where in the supply chain  people can't get  can't get labor to do the work that's  necessary and one of those impacts will  be wage inflation as people compete  for uh the workforce that is available  and that will have the long-term impact  on inflation in the uk economy and there  are other pressures there too there are  very significant commodity price  increases we all know about the gas  price and other fuel price increases so  that world food inflation at the moment  according to  two unl organizations is running at 20  per year there was a study in  agriculture in the uk last week that  showed that agricultural imp inflation  was over 30  now these are scary figures they won't  all feed through to the retail prices  index because there are lots of other  mitigations but they are a concern and  they are for the long term as is this  disruption  ian wright thank you very much indeed
 

